Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cambridge.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-15","committee":"Performance, Assets and Strategy Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cambridge.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-16","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cambridge.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-21","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cambridge.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-21","committee":"Services, Climate and Communities Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cambridge.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cambridge.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Rent regulation project ongoing through December 2026 to resolve tenant overcharging refunds","lead":"This represents financial exposure from prior control failures and means tenant arrears figures remain distorted until project completion.","iso":"2026-09-23","paper_title":"Q1 26-27 Performance report","paper_url":"https://democracy.cambridge.gov.uk/documents/s73588/73588.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Civic Quarter redevelopment decision in October creates budget uncertainty of \u00a30.8m income loss","lead":"Material budget uncertainty that could swing the council's financial position depending on a major capital project decision.","iso":"2026-09-23","paper_title":"Q1 26-27 Performance report","paper_url":"https://democracy.cambridge.gov.uk/documents/s73588/73588.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Investment income outperforming budget by \u00a30.329m due to higher interest rates lasting longer than expected","lead":"A positive offset to revenue pressures, showing the council is maximizing returns on cash reserves.","iso":"2026-09-23","paper_title":"Q1 26-27 Performance report","paper_url":"https://democracy.cambridge.gov.uk/documents/s73588/73588.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-23","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Q1 26-27 Performance report","paper_url":"https://democracy.cambridge.gov.uk/documents/s73588/73588.pdf","headline":"Rent regulation project ongoing through December 2026 to resolve tenant overcharging refunds","detail":"The council is working through refunds owed to tenants following prior overcharging of rents and service charges. The project will continue into at least December 2026 due to large number of refunds and account complexity. Both current and former tenant arrears are below target while this work proceeds. New software systems are being implemented to enable better account management.","category":"other","matters":"This represents financial exposure from prior control failures and means tenant arrears figures remain distorted until project completion.","figures":"Ongoing through at least December 2026","quote":"Continued to work through the refunds owed to tenants following the overcharging of rents and service charges. Due to the large number of refunds and complexity of some accounts this work will be ongoing into at least December 2026.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-23","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Q1 26-27 Performance report","paper_url":"https://democracy.cambridge.gov.uk/documents/s73588/73588.pdf","headline":"Civic Quarter redevelopment decision in October creates budget uncertainty of \u00a30.8m income loss","detail":"The council's budget contains contingent items dependent on Full Council approval of Civic Quarter redevelopment in October 2026. Corn Exchange venue closure from 1 January 2027 is forecast to create \u00a30.662m income loss, with \u00a30.154m Market Square project on hold pending decision. Should the project not proceed, significant income loss would still occur due to venue booking lead times.","category":"other","matters":"Material budget uncertainty that could swing the council's financial position depending on a major capital project decision.","figures":"\u00a30.662m Corn Exchange income loss; \u00a30.154m Market Square; decision scheduled October 2026","quote":"The Communities Group is showing 0.7m of additional cost, which reflects the  loss of income from the closure of the Corn Exchange venue from 1st January 2027, as part of the Civic Quarter redevelopment project.  Should the project not be approved by Full Council in October, there would still be a significant loss of income  due to the lead-in times for booking acts.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-23","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Q1 26-27 Performance report","paper_url":"https://democracy.cambridge.gov.uk/documents/s73588/73588.pdf","headline":"Investment income outperforming budget by \u00a30.329m due to higher interest rates lasting longer than expected","detail":"Council forecast investment income of \u00a31.8m for 2026/27 against budget of \u00a31.5m. The \u00a30.329m outperformance reflects Bank of England base rate at 3.75% persisting longer than anticipated at budget setting. Higher cash balances from capital programme delays have also contributed to higher average investment balances available.","category":"income","matters":"A positive offset to revenue pressures, showing the council is maximizing returns on cash reserves.","figures":"\u00a31.8m forecast versus \u00a31.5m budget; \u00a30.329m outperformance; base rate 3.75%","quote":"Because interest rates have remained higher for longer than anticipated, we are expecting a higher income from investments.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-23","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Q1 26-27 Performance report","paper_url":"https://democracy.cambridge.gov.uk/documents/s73588/73588.pdf","headline":"\u00a30.9m fire and damage costs plus \u00a30.5m for Awaab's law damp compliance and \u00a30.1m fire safety measures","detail":"The council is incurring significant unanticipated costs for fire damage (\u00a30.9m) and building compliance. Increased housing repairs spending (\u00a30.5m) is required to comply with Awaab's law on damp, condensation and mould, with sustained demand through winter. Interim fire safety measures including waking watch at properties cost \u00a30.1m, reduced from 11 sites to 2 but continuing through January 2027.","category":"overspend","matters":"These represent ongoing statutory compliance obligations driven by fire safety requirements and housing regulations that create continuing budget pressures not fully recoverable.","figures":"\u00a30.9m fire damage; \u00a30.5m Awaab's law compliance; \u00a30.1m waking watch through January 2027","quote":"\u00a30.9 million costs as a result of fire and other damage to properties, which could not be anticipated when budgets were set","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-23","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Q1 26-27 Performance report","paper_url":"https://democracy.cambridge.gov.uk/documents/s73588/73588.pdf","headline":"\u00a322.478m slippage on HRA capital programme delays housing delivery across multiple schemes","detail":"The HRA capital programme shows \u00a322.478m of underspend with budgets requested to carry forward to future years. Major delays include Princess and Hanover (\u00a37.573m, delayed by October 2026 CPO inquiry and planning complexity), Stanton House (\u00a33.469m), Davy Road (\u00a32.715m, planning submission delayed), and Ekin Road (\u00a31.930m). These delays affect housing supply delivery targets.","category":"capital","matters":"Housing delivery is central to the council's capital strategy and debt sustainability. Major scheme delays affect planned revenue streams and statutory housing obligations.","figures":"\u00a322.478m total slippage; \u00a37.573m Princess and Hanover; \u00a33.469m Stanton House; \u00a32.715m Davy Road","quote":"Within 2026/27, there is an overall underspend on the HRA capital programme. As at Q1, budget totalling \u00a322.478 million is anticipated to be requested to be carried forward into 2027/28 and subsequent years to allow projects to be completed.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-23"},"name":"Cambridge","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-25","since_iso":"2026-08-26","distress":false,"headline":"Rent regulation project ongoing through December 2026 to resolve tenant overcharging refunds","lead":"This represents financial exposure from prior control failures and means tenant arrears figures remain distorted until project completion.","also":["23 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Civic Affairs and Audit Committee on 2026-10-05","n_findings":24,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Q1 26-27 Performance report","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.cambridge.gov.uk/documents/s73588/73588.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":66,"news_drafts_total":3}}